# Line-ending policy — the release zip is staged straight from this working
# tree on EITHER dev machine, so checkout line endings become SHIPPED line
# endings. A Windows autocrlf checkout gave launcher.sh a CRLF shebang in the
# 1.1.6 zip, which silently broke launching on Linux/macOS (\r after "bash").
# Force LF for everything a Unix system executes or parses:
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
*.desktop   text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
# Windows-native scripts are safest with CRLF (cmd.exe quirks):
*.bat       text eol=crlf
